.TH DIFFM 1 "2026-09-19" "Diffmantic 0.8.0" "Diffmantic Manual"
.SH NAME
diffm \- structural, semantic diff engine powered by Tree-sitter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIFILE_A\fR \fIFILE_B\fR
.br
.B diffm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIREVISION\fR]
[\fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B diffm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
\fIREV_A\fR \fIREV_B\fR
.br
.B diffm
\fIPATH\fR \fIOLD_FILE\fR \fIOLD_HEX\fR \fIOLD_MODE\fR
\fINEW_FILE\fR \fINEW_HEX\fR \fINEW_MODE\fR
.br
.B diffm
[\fB\-\-parse\-tree\fR | \fB\-\-cst\fR]
\fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diffmantic
is a structural source code diff engine.
Instead of diffing files line-by-line, it parses source code into Abstract
Syntax Trees (ASTs) using Tree-sitter and tracks how language constructs
shift across revisions.
.PP
Diffmantic recognizes when entire functions, classes, methods, or blocks are
moved or reordered, when identifiers or expressions are updated in-place,
and when statements are inserted or deleted.
.PP
If a file exceeds size limits or contains parse errors beyond configured
thresholds, diffmantic falls back to line diffing so you always get a
usable diff.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-annotations\fR
.br
Include AST move annotations in diff (default: true)
.TP
\fB\-\-cached\fR
.br
Show only staged changes in Git mode
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR=\fIWHEN\fR
.br
Color output: always, never, auto (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-U\fR, \fB\-\-context\fR=\fILINES\fR
.br
Lines of context to show for diff (default: 3)
.TP
\fB\-\-cst\fR
.br
Dump the raw Tree-sitter concrete syntax tree instead of the Diffmantic
AST
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-sbs\fR
.br
Force strict 50/50 side-by-side rendering without adaptive hybrid inline
switching
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR=\fIFORMAT\fR
.br
Output format: side-by-side, inline, json, actions (default:
side-by-side)
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
.br
Include actions, line alignment, and highlight spans in JSON output
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
help for diffm
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-ignore\-comments\fR
.br
Ignore all comments when diffing
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-limit\fR=\fILINES\fR
.br
Maximum line count for AST parsing before falling back to line diff (0
to disable limit) (default: 10000)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-line\-numbers\fR
.br
Show line numbers in diff output (default: true)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
.br
Do not pipe output into a pager
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-parse\-error\-limit\fR=\fIN\fR
.br
Maximum parse errors allowed before falling back to line diffing
.TP
\fB\-\-parse\-tree\fR
.br
Parse files and dump the syntax tree for debugging
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-patch\fR
.br
Generate a standard patch suitable for git apply / patch tools
.TP
\fB\-\-size\-limit\fR=\fIKB\fR
.br
Maximum file size in KB for AST parsing before falling back to line diff
(0 to disable limit) (default: 1024)
.TP
\fB\-\-tab\-width\fR=\fIN\fR
.br
Number of spaces per tab stop in diff output (default: 4)
.TP
\fB\-\-textconv\fR
.br
Allow external text conversion filters to be run when comparing binary
files
.TP
\fB\-\-ui\fR
.br
Include line alignment and highlight spans in JSON output
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.br
version for diffm
.TP
\fB\-\-wrap\fR
.br
Wrap long lines to terminal width in inline diff
.TP
\fB\-\-wrap\-width\fR=\fICOLS\fR
.br
Explicit column width for line wrapping (0 to auto-detect terminal
width)
.SH GIT INTEGRATION
You can use
.B diffm
as a standalone command, or wire it directly into your Git workflow.
.SS Git Difftool
To configure diffmantic as your default Git difftool:
.PP
.nf
git config --global diff.tool diffm
git config --global difftool.diffm.cmd 'diffm "$LOCAL" "$REMOTE"'
git config --global difftool.prompt false
.fi
.PP
Then run:
.PP
.nf
git difftool
git difftool HEAD~1
.fi
.SS Git External Diff Driver
To use diffmantic whenever you run \fBgit diff\fR:
.PP
.nf
git config --global diff.external diffm
.fi
.PP
Diffmantic implements Git's 7-argument external diff driver protocol:
\fIpath old-file old-hex old-mode new-file new-hex new-mode\fR.
.SS File-Specific Driver via .gitattributes
To use diffmantic only for specific file types in a repository, add this to
your \fB.gitconfig\fR:
.PP
.nf
[diff "diffmantic"]
    command = diffm
.fi
.PP
And add this line to your repository's \fB.gitattributes\fR:
.PP
.nf
*.go diff=diffmantic
*.rs diff=diffmantic
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Diffmantic supports configuration via the following environment variables.
Command-line flags always take precedence over environment variables.
.TP
.B DIFFM_FORMAT
.br
Default diff output format (\fIside-by-side\fR, \fIinline\fR, \fIjson\fR,
\fIactions\fR).
.TP
.B DIFFM_TAB_WIDTH
.br
Number of spaces per tab stop (default: 4).
.TP
.B DIFFM_IGNORE_COMMENTS
.br
Boolean (\fI1\fR, \fItrue\fR, \fIyes\fR) to ignore comments during AST
diffing (default: 0).
.TP
.B DIFFM_PARSE_ERROR_LIMIT
.br
Maximum parse errors permitted before falling back to line diffing
(default: 0).
.TP
.B DIFFM_SIZE_LIMIT
.br
Maximum file size in KB for AST parsing before fallback (default: 1024).
.TP
.B DIFFM_LINE_LIMIT
.br
Maximum line count for AST parsing before fallback (default: 10000).
.TP
.B DIFFM_NO_PAGER
.br
If set to any non-empty value, disables the interactive terminal pager.
.SH SUPPORTED LANGUAGES
Diffmantic includes native Tree-sitter parsers for 10 programming languages:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGo\fR (\fI.go\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBJava\fR (\fI.java\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBJavaScript\fR (\fI.js\fR, \fI.jsx\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTypeScript\fR (\fI.ts\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBTSX\fR (\fI.tsx\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPython\fR (\fI.py\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRust\fR (\fI.rs\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBZig\fR (\fI.zig\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBC\fR (\fI.c\fR, \fI.h\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBC++\fR (\fI.cpp\fR, \fI.cc\fR, \fI.hpp\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLua\fR (\fI.lua\fR)
.PP
Files in other languages fall back automatically to standard line diffing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.br
Success. Files were diffed, syntax trees were dumped, or files are identical.
.TP
.B 1
.br
Differences detected or an error occurred (such as invalid arguments,
unreadable files, or internal parsing failures).
.SH EXAMPLES
Compare two local Go files side-by-side with an interactive pager:
.PP
.RS
diffm old.go new.go
.RE
.PP
Print an AST-aware inline diff:
.PP
.RS
diffm -f inline old.rs new.rs
.RE
.PP
Generate an inline patch suitable for patch tools:
.PP
.RS
diffm -p old.py new.py
.RE
.PP
Inspect unstaged working directory changes in a Git repository:
.PP
.RS
diffm
.RE
.PP
Inspect staged changes only:
.PP
.RS
diffm --cached
.RE
.PP
Compare two Git branches or commits:
.PP
.RS
diffm main feature-branch
.RE
.PP
Compare a single file between commits:
.PP
.RS
diffm HEAD~1 src/server.go
.RE
.PP
Export structured JSON for editor integration (Neovim, VS Code):
.PP
.RS
diffm --ui -f json old.go new.go
.RE
.PP
Dump the simplified AST for debugging parser output:
.PP
.RS
diffm --parse-tree main.go
.RE
